.TH CVECTOR_POP_BACK 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cvector_pop_back \- remove and return the last element from the vector
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

ccol_retval_t cvector_pop_back(cvec v, void *target_elem);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Removes the last element of the vector and copies it into the target
buffer. When that leaves the vector less than 1/4 full, the capacity is
halved, down to the minimum of 4.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v            Vector to pop from
target_elem  Pointer to the buffer that receives the element (must not
             be NULL)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success        - The element was popped
ccol_invalid_args   - target_elem is NULL
ccol_container_empty - The vector is empty
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
O(1). The element is copied into target_elem, and the capacity halves
when the vector is less than 1/4 full, never going below 4. Asserts if v
is NULL.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvector_push_back (3),
.BR cvec_pop (3)
